WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.559
IT and OT use many of the same technologies, but they serve different missions.

00:00:06.559 --> 00:00:11.849
Enterprise IT supports communication, business applications, identity, analytics, and data processing.

00:00:11.849 --> 00:00:16.292
OT supports the observation and control of physical operations.

00:00:16.292 --> 00:00:22.428
That difference changes how risk is evaluated and how security work is performed.

00:00:22.428 --> 00:00:26.871
IT systems are often refreshed on relatively short cycles.

00:00:26.871 --> 00:00:37.662
OT equipment may remain in service for decades because it is integrated with expensive machinery, certified processes, or infrastructure that cannot be replaced casually.

00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:44.644
Older controllers and workstations may use unsupported operating systems or protocols with little built-in security.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:49.510
Replacement may require engineering redesign, procurement, testing, and an outage.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:52.261
Patching also carries different constraints.

00:00:52.261 --> 00:01:01.359
An IT team may deploy updates during a routine maintenance window and recover a failed endpoint from a standard image.

00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:10.457
In OT, a change may require a planned shutdown, vendor participation, process testing, safety approval, and a verified rollback method.

00:01:10.457 --> 00:01:18.286
A controller reboot at the wrong time can interrupt production or leave equipment in an undesirable state.

00:01:18.286 --> 00:01:25.268
Availability requirements can be strict, but “never touch the system” is not a security strategy.

00:01:25.268 --> 00:01:30.981
OT teams still need vulnerability management, access control, monitoring, and lifecycle planning.

00:01:30.981 --> 00:01:35.001
The controls must be adapted to the process.

00:01:35.001 --> 00:01:39.021
Passive discovery may be preferable to aggressive scanning.

00:01:39.021 --> 00:01:43.887
Network containment may reduce risk while a patch awaits testing.

00:01:43.887 --> 00:01:47.907
Compensating controls need owners, evidence, and expiration criteria.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:53.620
IT assumptions should therefore be tested before they are applied to OT.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:59.333
Automated isolation, endpoint enforcement, or credential changes can have unexpected operational effects.

00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:04.622
At the same time, OT cannot remain disconnected from enterprise governance.

00:02:04.622 --> 00:02:09.912
Modern operations depend on remote support, analytics, vendors, and business systems.

00:02:09.912 --> 00:02:16.048
The strongest programs combine IT security expertise with engineering knowledge and operational authority.
